[FINAL-TEXT] === DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
I could not reproduce any cross-fabric outage. End-to-end data plane between racks is healthy:
- Reachability: pc_0_0 -> pc_0_1 and pc_0_1 -> pc_0_0 both show 0% loss with ~2–3 ms RTTs.
- Throughput: iperf from pc_0_0 to pc_0_1 sustained ~54–60 Mbit/s for 3 seconds with 0 retransmits, indicating a stable path.

Control plane across the “middle” (spines and super-spine) is up and exchanging routes:
- leaf_router_0_0 installs 10.0.1.0/24 via 172.16.0.4 (eth0) and leaf_router_0_1 installs 10.0.0.0/24 via 172.16.0.6 (eth0). 
- Both spines learn 10.0.0.0/24 and 10.0.1.0/24 over BGP and have next-hops toward the correct leaves. 
- super_spine_router_0 has established BGP sessions to both spines and is advertising/receiving prefixes (neighbors in Established state, nonzero PfxRcd/PfxSnt).

Mechanism: With BGP sessions established across leaves–spines–super-spine, both /24 host networks are present in the RIB/FIB, so traffic forwards correctly through the core (ECMP-capable) fabric.

Localization: All involved devices—leaf_router_0_0, leaf_router_0_1, spine_router_0_0, spine_router_0_1, and super_spine_router_0—show healthy BGP and correct routes. No interface or daemon fault observed.

Root cause: Not a current network issue; the reported symptom is not reproducible.

Corrective fix: No changes required. Please retry your workflows. If problems recur, capture exact timestamps and affected ports/protocols so we can correlate with control-plane logs and host-level services (e.g., DNS/firewall/app listeners). 
